# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Aadhaar Verification Service — .gitignore
#
# ⛔ THE RULE THIS FILE EXISTS TO ENFORCE
#
#    No Aadhaar data ever enters git. Not an image, not a decoded payload, not
#    a number, not a name. Git history is effectively permanent — it survives in
#    every clone, every fork and every CI cache, and `git rm` does not remove it
#    from history. A mistake here cannot be undone by deleting the file later.
#
#    Everything below that carries a ⛔ is a privacy or security rule. The rest
#    is ordinary housekeeping.
#
# ⚠ WHAT MUST *NOT* BE IGNORED
#
#    certs/*.cer, certs/*.pem      UIDAI PUBLIC certificates. They are the trust
#                                  store and they belong in the repo.
#    certs/FINGERPRINTS.txt        The pin file. Committing it is what makes
#                                  trust-store tampering detectable.
#    tenants.json                  Holds only tenant ids and the NAMES of
#                                  environment variables — never a secret.
#
#    There is deliberately no blanket `*.pem` rule, because it would silently
#    exclude the trust store and nobody would notice until a deploy had no
#    certificates and every genuine card returned ERROR.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⛔ AADHAAR DATA — the rules that matter most
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The local image corpus. Lives OUTSIDE the repo by design (C:\aadhaar-corpus),
# but these patterns catch a copy accidentally dropped inside it.
aadhaar-corpus/
corpus/
**/aadhaar-corpus/
*aadhaar*.jpg
*aadhaar*.jpeg
*aadhaar*.png
*aadhaar*.heic

# UIDAI's published sample payload. Fetched by scripts/fetch_spec_sample.py.
# It decodes to a real person's demographics and photograph, so even though
# UIDAI published it, it does not enter this repository.
tests/fixtures/local/

# Reports generated from the real corpus. No personal data by design — they
# emit counts, error codes and field SHAPES only — but they are derived from
# real cards and are pure noise in a diff. Regenerate any time.
report.txt
diagnosis.txt
corpus_report.txt
*.corpus.txt

# Decoded QR payloads. A payload IS the signed demographic record.
*.payload.txt
payloads/

# Cropped QR regions written by scripts/diagnose_failures.py --save-crops.
# ⛔ A crop of an Aadhaar QR IS the signed demographic record in image form —
#    more directly readable than the full card, not less. Stays local.
_crops/
**/_crops/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⛔ SECRETS AND KEYS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Private keys, anywhere, under any name. A committed key is a compromised key
# — rotating it does not remove it from history.
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*_private.pem
*-private.pem
id_rsa*

# Real environment files. `.env.example` IS committed — it documents the
# variable names with placeholder values and nothing else.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The tenant registry holds only variable NAMES, so it is committable. A file
# named for a specific environment probably holds real values.
tenants.*.json
tenants.local.json

# demo/ is entirely generated by scripts/make_demo_document.py and contains a
# throwaway signing key. ⛔ Its certificate must NEVER reach certs/ — anything
# signed with that key would verify, which is exactly the trust-store poisoning
# that FINGERPRINTS.txt exists to prevent.
demo/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated output — reproducible, so not worth tracking
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `avs preprocess` writes preprocessing variants here. Derived from whatever
# image you pointed it at — which may have been a real card.
variants/

# `scripts/make_test_image.py` regenerates these on demand.
test-images/

# Audit trails. Real verdict records: no personal data, but operational state
# that belongs on the server, not in source control.
#
# ⚠ ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, deliberately. An unanchored `audit/` matches
#   at ANY depth, so it silently excluded `src/avs/audit/` — the entire audit
#   module source. Caught by the check below; it would otherwise have surfaced
#   as an ImportError on a fresh clone, long after the commit that caused it.
/audit/
audit.jsonl
*.audit.jsonl
local_e2e_audit.jsonl
mock_hrm_audit.jsonl
test_page_audit.jsonl


# AI model weights — Step 12. A model file is tens to hundreds of megabytes and
# git history is permanent, so a blob committed once is carried by every clone
# forever. Models are distributed separately and verified by digest.
#
# ⚠ models.json is NOT ignored, deliberately. It holds only names, versions and
#   SHA-256 digests, and committing it is precisely what makes a swapped model
#   file detectable — the same reasoning as certs/FINGERPRINTS.txt.
*.onnx
*.ort
*.pt
*.safetensors
models/*.onnx
!models/models.json


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
ENV/

build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Node — Step 11 Next.js integration
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Java — Step 10 Spring integration
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

target/
*.class
*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
.gradle/
build/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors and operating systems
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs and scratch
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.log
logs/
tmp/
scratch/
